 "title": "Hayes County Register of Deeds",
 "text": "Hayes County Register of Deeds\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nHome\nCounty\nAbout\nHistory\nOffices\nAssessor\nAssessor's\nOffice\nHomestead Exemptions\nPersonal Property Info\nAttorney\nBoard of Commissioners\nBoard Members\nMeeting Agenda\nMeeting Minutes\nClerk\nClerk's Office\nBirth Certificate Info\nMarriage License\nMilitary\nDischarge\nProperty Valuation\nProtests\nSpecial\nLicenses\nCounty Court\nClerk of the District Court\nDistrict\nCourt Office\nCourt Filing Fees\nSelf Help\nElection Commissioner\nElection Commissioner's\nOffice\nElection Information\nSecretary of State\nLocal\nElection Results\nEmergency Manager\nExtension Office\nHighway Department\nPlanning and Zoning\nRegister of\nDeeds\nSheriff\nSurveyor\nTreasurer\nTreasurer's\nOffice\nBoating Guide\nBoating Registration\nDriver's\nExam\nDrivers Licenses\nFAQ's\nProperty Tax Payments\nTitles and Registration\nUnclaimed Property\nVeterans Services Officer\nWeed Superintendent\nCalendar\nContacts\nOffice Links\nCommunity\nLinks\nServices Offered\nFeedback\n-->\nRegister of Deeds\nOffice Hours\n8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.\nPhone\n(308) 286-3413\nFax\n(308) 286-3208\nAddress\nP.O. Box 370\n505 Troth Street\nHayes Center, NE 69032\nLinks\nCounty Clerk\nNebraska Form 521 fill-in form\nNebraska Form 521MH fill-in form\nSusan Messersmith\n|\nHayes County Register of Deeds\n|\nRebecca Grimes\n|\nDeputy\n|\nThe Register is responsible for receiving and recording all legal\ndocuments affecting Real Estate within Hayes County.\nALL INSTRUMENTS ; ( Effective\nJan. 1, 2013, LB14) e.g., Deeds, Construction\nLiens, Mortgages, Lis Pendens, Releases, Affidavits, Contracts,\nAssignments, etc. are figured on the basis of $10.00 for the first page,\nplus $6.00 for each additional page (front and back count as two\npages). There are no fees charged for lots or sections of\nland.\nSPACE REQUIREMENT , as set forth in § 23-1503.1:\nA 3\" x 8 1/2\" space at the TOP of the FIRST PAGE of each\ninstrument for recording shall be left blank for recording\ninformation ONLY. If this space is not provided, The Register\nof Deeds is authorized to attach an extra sheet of paper to the\ninstrument, placing it as the first page, and charge an additional\n$6.00 in recording fee. Note: Taping to an 8 1/2\" x 11\"\ndocument to create sufficient space is not permitted.\nDOCUMENTARY STAMP TAX on deeds is $2.25 per\nthousand dollars of actual purchase price on transactions that are\nnot exempt under state statute. If the property transfers for\nnominal consideration, documentary stamp tax will be collected on\nassessed value.\nNebraska Documentary Stamp Tax Computation Table\nUCC FILING FEES : $14 for the first page of\neach initial financing statement, amendment, assignment,\ncontinuation statement, partial release or correction statement. $.50 for each additional page.\nThere is no fee for recording termination statements.\nFEDERAL TAX and STATE LIENS have to be recorded\nin the secretary of state's office first, then the secretary of\nstate forwards them to the register of deeds.\nCERTIFIED COPIES : $1.50 for each page of the\ncopy.\nCopyright © 2010 MIPS Inc. All rights reserved. |\nDisclaimer\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate",
